  "question": {
    "text": "An urn contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> white and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math> black balls. Two successive draws of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> balls are made without replacement. The probability, that the first draw gives all white balls and the second draw gives all black balls, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "oPaDq",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>256</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Hr3Lz",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>715</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hkDQo",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>715</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1gybS",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>256</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Total number of balls in the bag <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>.</p><p>Number of white balls <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p><p>Number of black balls <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.</p><p>Four balls are drawn at random at a time.</p><p>The probability that first draw give four white balls</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>6</mn></mmultiscripts><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>15</mn></mmultiscripts></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>91</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>The balls are not replaced.</p><p>Now, the probability that second draw give four black balls</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>11</mn></mmultiscripts></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>55</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>The probability that the first draw give four white balls  and second draw give four black balls</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>91</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>55</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>715</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the required probability is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>715</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
